beamSolid: standalone beam mechanics through solids4Foam
=======================================================

Validated with OpenFOAM.com v2412, double precision, 32-bit labels, serial.
v2306, v2312 and v2512 are future validation targets, not verified versions.

Build
-----
From the solids4foam root, after sourcing OpenFOAM and building the existing
solids4foam libraries and ThirdParty Eigen dependency:

    src/beamModels/Allwmake
    src/beamSolid/Allwmake
    applications/utilities/createBeamMesh/Allwmake
    applications/utilities/setInitialPositionBeam/Allwmake

The normal Allwmake also includes these targets for OpenFOAM.com when
S4F_NO_USE_EIGEN is unset. OpenFOAM.org and foam-extend builds skip them.
The beam libraries are loaded by the case; solids4Foam.C is unchanged.
Do not load the original libwireBunchingModels alongside the migrated library.

Case configuration
------------------
system/controlDict:

    application solids4Foam;
    libs ("libS4FBeamSolid.so");
    startFrom startTime;
    startTime 0;

constant/physicsProperties:

    type solid;

constant/solidProperties:

    solidModel beamSolid;
    beamSolidCoeffs
    {
        solutionAlgorithm implicitCoupled;
        infoFrequency 1;
    }

Retain constant/beamProperties and the W and Theta initial fields. Add a
constant/g uniformDimensionedVectorField as required by solidModel; use zero
for cases without gravity. Beam solver tolerances and material/section data
remain in beamProperties. No continuum mechanicalProperties file is needed.

Change beam boundary types fixedDisplacement and fixedRotation to
beamFixedDisplacement and beamFixedRotation, respectively. Other beam
boundary types keep their original names.

Mesh and fields
---------------
Use createBeamMesh, followed by setInitialPositionBeam when needed. The solid
base loads this BEAM mesh. The embedded beam model borrows the same dynamicFvMesh;
it does not construct a continuum mesh. Both use pointMesh::New for a common
point-mesh wrapper. Points, faces, cell zones and cross-section data are retained.

W and Theta remain the primary beam fields. pointW includes cross-section
rotation. The adapter updates inherited D/DD and pointD/pointDD for the solid
interface and returns the beam U field. It suppresses unused continuum stress
output and delegates field writing to beamFoam. Continuum traction boundary
conditions are rejected; use the beam force and moment boundary conditions.
The original fixed-step application behavior is retained.

Tutorials
---------
Run ./Allrun in any of these directories under tutorials/solids/beamsPlatesShells:

    beamCantilever
    beamDynamicCantilever
    beamFollowerForce

The dynamic tutorial includes the original initial-rotation utility step.
All tutorials start at zero and do not require plotting software.

Validation and limits
---------------------
Three clean original/migrated pairs were run from time zero. All 2700 written
field files matched exactly after normalising the two boundary type names.
All 11 displacement, force/moment, energy and convergence history files matched
byte-for-byte. The imported mesh utility produced byte-identical points,
connectivity, boundary and zone files for the cantilever. The existing continuum
patchTest also passed with libS4FBeamSolid loaded, exercising the original
continuum fixedDisplacement boundary condition alongside the beam versions.

DYNAMIC RESTART IS NOT VALIDATED FOR CONTINUOUS-RUN EQUIVALENCE. Restarting at
0.5 reproduced the original beamFoam restarted result exactly, but both differed
from an uninterrupted run. The original model marks dynamic state fields such
as U, Accl, Omega and dotOmega NO_WRITE. This migration preserves that behavior.
Use uninterrupted runs from time zero until restart-state persistence is fixed
and separately validated. Setting the inherited solidModel restart switch does
not make the beam state restart-complete.

Fluid coupling, multiple regions, parallel execution and optional spring,
contact and wave/Morison loading are outside the validated first phase. Existing
optional implementation files remain in the imported library to preserve its
dependencies; their presence is not a claim of validated integration.

Comprehensive migration summary
-------------------------------
See ../../docs/beamFoam-migration-summary.txt for the architecture, file-level
changes, build/case setup, validation evidence, and remaining limitations.

